<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 19:13:00 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>US firm to take over some Venezuela oilfields previously run by Chinese, Russian firms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-firm-to-take-over-some-venezuela-oilfields-previously-run-by-chinese-russian-firms</link><description>
The White House on Monday said it’s partnering with North American Blue Energy Partners as part of President Donald Trump’s push to tap into Venezuela’s oil industry, setting up a deal that will give the Pentagon a stake over roughly a fifth of the country’s vast oil reserves. Venezuela's ruling party-dominated ​National Assembly backed the ​country's oil deal with the Trump administration in a vote on ​Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a6a7b4ac-0cf1-11f1-b031-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-13T165204Z-1701345975-RC2BICA0A29K-RTRMADP-3-VENEZUELA-USA-OIL-EXPORTS-EXCLUSIVE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a6a7b4ac-0cf1-11f1-b031-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-13T165204Z-1701345975-RC2BICA0A29K-RTRMADP-3-VENEZUELA-USA-OIL-EXPORTS-EXCLUSIVE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0b778ba-a635-11f1-9b4c-af91c05e98b9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 19:00:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mass burials held in Nepal as bodies wash up after catastrophic flooding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mass-burials-held-in-nepal-as-bodies-wash-up-after-catastrophic-flooding</link><description>
Every day, new bodies are recovered in Nepal, but many remain unidentifiable. Several days after the disaster, some are already in an advanced state of decomposition. Morgues in the country's main cities are reaching capacity. Faced with the influx of remains, authorities have begun burying them without formal identification. France 24's special correspondents traveled to Bharatpur, in southern Nepal, to one of these burial sites.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f70db168-a633-11f1-8dfc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260901-200150-200343-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f70db168-a633-11f1-8dfc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260901-200150-200343-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fca13ff0-a633-11f1-a97d-af91c05e98b9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 18:40:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>School without screens: Will France's high school phone ban fly?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260901-school-wihout-screens-will-france-s-high-school-phone-ban-fly</link><description>
A lot happened during summer recess: France’s constitutional council struck down the core of a new law to ban social media for under 15 year olds, but it did validate the extension to high schoolers of a phone ban already in effect for younger pupils. Why one but not the other? On this the first day of school across this country and others, we’ll size up what's best for future citizens, parents and teachers… all grappling in this age of distraction with the lure of screens. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/832fcf50-a62f-11f1-86d5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-01T114337Z-351438158-RC2BANAPXXP8-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-SCHOOL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/832fcf50-a62f-11f1-86d5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-01T114337Z-351438158-RC2BANAPXXP8-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-SCHOOL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ed1fbf8-a62e-11f1-b898-b30d8ae45997</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 18:23:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lindsay Clancy: The trial putting postpartum mental illness in the spotlight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-lindsay-clancy-the-trial-putting-postpartum-mental-illness-in-the-spotlight</link><description>
Jurors in the murder trial of Lindsay Clancy notified the judge ​on September 1 that they were unable to reach a unanimous decision on whether to convict her for killing her three young children at her home in ​2023 – a ‌tragedy her attorney contends occurred while she was suffering ⁠from postpartum psychosis. FRANCE 24 takes a closer look at this case, which has sparked fevered debate in the United States over postpartum mental health. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9927719a-a626-11f1-88e7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-30.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9927719a-a626-11f1-88e7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-30.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">034c333a-a627-11f1-9070-b30d8ae45997</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 17:11:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany blames Russia for Leipzig airport drone attack, orders Russian consulate closed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-germany-blames-russia-for-leipzig-airport-drone-attack-orders-russian-consulate-closed</link><description>
Germany's government on Tuesday blamed Russia for an attempted attack at Leipzig/Halle Airport on 4 August using an explosive-laden drone, and announced that it would shut down a Russian consulate among other measures against Moscow. French ​President Emmanuel Macron ​said he supported the ​adoption ‌of ⁠new European sanctions ‌against Russia after the attempted drone attack.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0569ab12-a626-11f1-8099-df4aff4c5350</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 17:00:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg">© Axel Schmidt, Reuters </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What to know about the new UK PM's agenda as he faces lawmakers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-new-uk-pm-s-agenda-as-he-faces-lawmakers</link><description>
Since taking office on July 20, Burnham has traveled around the country promising to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of his predecessor Keir Starmer. Now, it's time for him to face lawmakers for the first time since he has taken office after an unusually long time without having to do so due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us what to know from his speech.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cc3533c-8438-11f1-98fd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T120731Z-1505653970-RC2NHMAGF2Z5-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cc3533c-8438-11f1-98fd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T120731Z-1505653970-RC2NHMAGF2Z5-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a6e7780-a619-11f1-8968-db76c1323643</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:39:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany set to blame Russia for airport explosive-laden drone incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-germany-set-to-blame-russia-for-airport-explosive-laden-drone-incident</link><description>
Berlin is set to formally blame Russia for an incident involving drones at a strategic airport on the night of August 4-5, including one that was found carrying explosives. Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul and Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt are expected to accuse a Russian intelligence service of being behind the incident. It would be the first time Germany formally blames Moscow for an incident like this one.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad1f73ce-a616-11f1-9b43-8d73d79a9abf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:35:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Replay: UK PM Andy Burnham faces lawmakers for first time since taking office</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/replay-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time-since-taking-office</link><description>
Rewatch UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham's first speech to parliament since taking office six weeks prior.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80a63c86-a618-11f1-b626-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1891369266a96ecf6cd7717-90115964.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80a63c86-a618-11f1-b626-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1891369266a96ecf6cd7717-90115964.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">09332ec6-a617-11f1-8c3d-db76c1323643</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:22:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Niger's thwarted mutiny highlights junta's dependence on Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260901-what-russia-helping-niger-junta-stop-mutiny-means-for-its-sovereignty</link><description>
A failed mutiny in Niger over the weekend shows how important Russia's Africa Corps mercenaries are in the country, according to analysts. They argue that the failed mutiny on Saturday shows how the country's security landscape has worsened and contradicts claims from Niger's junta about the country's independence from foreign powers. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dee046c-a610-11f1-ab0a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36LJ3WE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dee046c-a610-11f1-ab0a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36LJ3WE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1254274-a60f-11f1-9f90-afc18f454785</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:16:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dee046c-a610-11f1-ab0a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36LJ3WE.jpg">© Yuri Kochetkov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>From North Korea to ICE: Photojournalist David Guttenfelder on the front lines in Minneapolis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260901-from-north-korea-to-ice-photojournalist-david-guttenfelder-on-the-front-lines-in-minneapolis</link><description>
David Guttenfelder from The New York Times has spent 35 years photographing history around the world. Now, he is documenting it at home. The award-winning photojournalist is known for his work in Rwanda, North Korea and conflict zones across the globe. This year, he turned his camera on Minneapolis, documenting the federal immigration crackdown and deadly clashes involving ICE. His exhibition "The People of Minneapolis vs. ICE" is currently on show at the Visa pour l'Image photojournalism festival in Perpignan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c35a6c54-a614-11f1-ac7d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14795033246a96e6b0b762a9-82489987.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c35a6c54-a614-11f1-ac7d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14795033246a96e6b0b762a9-82489987.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3194d856-a617-11f1-b901-db76c1323643</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:10:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Eve JACKSON</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>After 'unprecedented honeymoon', UK PM faces lawmakers for first time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/after-unprecedented-honeymoon-uk-pm-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time</link><description>
Prime Minister Andy Burnham will face lawmakers in the House of Commons on September 1 for the first time since becoming UK leader six weeks ago. This comes as the wars in Europe and the Middle East weighing on his promise to kick-start the economy and ease the cost of living. Andy Burnham has enjoyed quite a long time without facing lawmakers due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5dc73ba-84a7-11f1-a0fa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201430781165.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5dc73ba-84a7-11f1-a0fa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201430781165.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a49f9ae-a615-11f1-ada6-21b4b9529c13</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:10:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Alejandro Betancourt, the controversial Venezuelan oil tycoon Trump is banking on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-alejandro-betancourt-the-controversial-venezuelan-oil-tycoon-trump-is-banking-on</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Friday announced "the biggest oil deal in world history" – a new deal with Venezuela for "65 billion barrels of oil". Washington is set to take a 35 percent stake in North American Blue Energy Partners, which is owned by controversial Venezuelan oil tycoon Alejandro Betancourt.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/102ed6f2-a555-11f1-8731-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/alejandroBetancourt.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/102ed6f2-a555-11f1-8731-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/alejandroBetancourt.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4300a362-a604-11f1-9def-cdea27736d9b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:05:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/102ed6f2-a555-11f1-8731-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/alejandroBetancourt.jpg">© France Médias Monde graphics studio</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>At least 12 killed and over a dozen injured in Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/at-least-12-killed-and-over-a-dozen-injured-in-russian-strikes-on-kyiv</link><description>
Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured many more in Kyiv and the surrounding region early on September 1, authorities said, marking the sixth straight day of intense strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Those injured three children, just as Ukrainian pupils return to school. In a new tactic, Moscow has sent swarms of new jet-powered drones to ⁠plague Kyiv and nearby areas day and night, killing residents and damaging homes and warehouses.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33f40dfc-a5f3-11f1-a5be-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-01T100315Z-704783314-RC2AANAPA26V-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33f40dfc-a5f3-11f1-a5be-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-01T100315Z-704783314-RC2AANAPA26V-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ee3246c-a612-11f1-851d-8d73d79a9abf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:56:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Child sex abuse scandals loom over France as pupils head back to school</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/child-sex-abuse-scandals-loom-over-france-as-pupils-head-back-to-school</link><description>
In France, children headed back to school on September 1. But this year, parents had more to worry about than packing backpacks and getting them there on time. Several months ago, news broke of hundreds of sexual assault and rape allegations against monitors at schools and childcare centres in Paris. Monitors are employed by local authorities for after-school care and also look after the children before classes begin and during breaks. Parents want the government to provide safety guarantees.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e7d1bc6-a613-11f1-80ac-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260901-161033-161216-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e7d1bc6-a613-11f1-80ac-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260901-161033-161216-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">53c940e6-a613-11f1-9c4b-8d73d79a9abf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:54:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Controversial designer John Galliano cancels Met exhibition after backlash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/controversial-designer-john-galliano-cancels-met-exhibition-after-backlash</link><description>
John Galliano has cancelled an upcoming major exhibition celebrating his work as a fashion designer after it prompted criticism due to his previous conviction for making antisemitic remarks. In 2011, a French court found the designer guilty of antisemitic and racist rants at a Parisian bar. He was also fired by Dior as creative director that same year after a video surfaced of him declaring a love for Hitler.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04fc2016-a611-11f1-9d24-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12252336376a96e068e587e2-89761582.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04fc2016-a611-11f1-9d24-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12252336376a96e068e587e2-89761582.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee202d40-a608-11f1-bee0-cdea27736d9b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:28:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French astronaut takes third spacewalk outside ISS in all-female mission</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-astronaut-takes-third-spacewalk-outside-iss-in-all-female-mission</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot is taking her third spacewalk in two weeks and is leading rare all-female excursion outside ISS. The main mission is to replace a retroreflector, a device that align modules when they arrive towards the space station. Other maintenance operations are planned. The whole excursion is supposed to last between six and six and a half hours. It is only the sixth all-female excursion in space history.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f51ae1c-a60d-11f1-8c32-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16351816906a96da653eb2b6-05430368.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f51ae1c-a60d-11f1-8c32-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16351816906a96da653eb2b6-05430368.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14d4947c-a60d-11f1-b591-afc18f454785</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:19:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>After the floods, Nepal works to bury hundreds of washed-up unidentified bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-works-to-bury-hundreds-of-washed-up-unidentified-bodies</link><description>
Nepal is burying dozens of bodies in multiple trenches as Nepal’s disaster agency said that 1,003 deaths had been counted there, with 3,916 people missing, including 583 foreign nationals. In its latest update, China reported 16 deaths and 546 missing, including 261 foreigners. Crews faced challenging conditions as they searched unstable terrain and piles of debris. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a7435174-a476-11f1-ad38-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T132655Z-836715202-RC209NA6ORCP-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-MASSBURIAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a7435174-a476-11f1-ad38-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T132655Z-836715202-RC209NA6ORCP-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-MASSBURIAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f853d4b2-a606-11f1-aceb-77a48fff9120</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:08:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ghana cocoa farmers reject new 'punitive' land conversion law</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-ghana-cocoa-farmers-reject-new-punitive-land-conversion-law</link><description>
Ghanaian cocoa farmers are ramping up their pushback against a new law preventing them from using their land for anything else without permission. President Mahama says supporting local processing is the key to economic growth. Cocoa chiefs say that the changes still leave the sector resting on an outdated colonial model.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66e10e78-90a8-11f1-b54b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26066850241444.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66e10e78-90a8-11f1-b54b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26066850241444.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84c2b0ce-a5eb-11f1-aa0b-53703fbaf52c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:05:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal's rescuers navigate mud-swamped tunnels for hundreds of missing workers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-s-rescuers-navigate-mud-swamped-tunnels-for-hundreds-of-missing-workers</link><description>
The death toll in Nepal has crossed 1,000 from the deadly floods that tore through an area on the border with Tibet on August 26, and nearly 4,000 people remain missing. six days on hopes for survivors are dimming, but rescuers focused on a network of hydropower sites along the Trishuli River are holding out hope. Of the roughly 900 workers missing, some 500 people are believed to be trapped in the tunnels, according to Nepalese authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f37cc1f0-a517-11f1-b844-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VW7CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f37cc1f0-a517-11f1-b844-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VW7CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">04b62fcc-a605-11f1-863b-f9580e1f490b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:59:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>From sexual violence to mobile phones, what's changing for French pupils?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/from-sexual-violence-to-mobile-phones-what-s-changing-for-french-pupils</link><description>
Millions of French students are heading back to school this week and with that comes a host of new rules for what will be the last school year of Emmanuel Macron's presidency. From phone bans to exam schedules, Camille Knight takes a look at what's changing in the French school system, and why those changes are being put in place.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c28061c8-a5e0-11f1-b00f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6YK8GT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c28061c8-a5e0-11f1-b00f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6YK8GT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac019462-a603-11f1-8d79-cdea27736d9b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:56:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Jury convicts former gang member of rapper Tupac Shakur's murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/jury-convicts-former-gang-member-of-rapper-tupac-shakur-s-murder</link><description>
Twelve jurors found former gangster Duane "Keffe D" Davis guilty of the murder of Tupac Shakur in Nevada's Clark County court on August 31. Although the 63 year-old is not thought to have fired the deadly shots himself, he is the only man still alive out of those who were in the car at the time. Under Nevada law, someone who helps another person commit murder can be convicted of the crime.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f9a702-a59c-11f1-8391-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243678304338.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f9a702-a59c-11f1-8391-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243678304338.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5437869c-a603-11f1-9bba-cdea27736d9b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:52:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia's G20 US invitation severely criticised by European countries</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-g20-us-invitation-severely-criticised-by-european-countries</link><description>
Finance ministers and central bank governors from the group of 20 major economies are meeting for two days in Asheville, North Carolina. With the United States holding the rotating G20 presidency, Washington is trying to rally partners towards greater economic pressure on Iran and find ways to boost growth. But an unexpected attendee drew fierce criticism.
