In DR Congo, managing the spread of Ebola is made all the more difficult as the country is juggling simultaneous security crises including untangling a peace deal with M23 rebels. President Felix Tshisekedi offered to convene a national dialogue which opposition parties call a smoke screen hiding an attempted power grab.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f3eb084-a60a-11f1-87d6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26163611421863.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f3eb084-a60a-11f1-87d6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26163611421863.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">85ce0d0a-a5e7-11f1-8c92-530b91485ab7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:40:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine hopes for bolstered support as EU defence ministers meet in Dublin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hopes-for-bolstered-support-as-eu-defence-ministers-meet-in-dublin</link><description>
EU defence ministers grapple with bolstering Ukraine's air defences, as worries grow over Russia's campaign to destabilise Kyiv's European backers. This comes as Moscow is taking advantage of Kyiv running low on US-built air defence missiles to intensify its attacks on the country. EU ministers are also expected to discuss Russia's hybrid war against Ukraine's European allies. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley tells us more.
